Ladybird counts a font’s ascent and descent in whole pixels in layout,
and puts the floor of the leading above the text and the rest below.
Blink does the same: FontMetrics::AscentDescentWithHacks() rounds the
font’s ascent and descent with SkScalarRoundToScalar(), except for
tiny fonts, and CalculateLeadingSpace() gives the ascent side
((line_height - height) / 2).Floor() and the descent side the rest.
